# Package layering (AiT toolbox — ai-ssh)

Authoritative detail: [docs/package-layering.md](../../docs/package-layering.md) · [docs/package-layering.zh-CN.md](../../docs/package-layering.zh-CN.md). Keep this rule in sync when those docs change.

## Call chain

`cmd/ai-ssh` → `internal/ai-ssh` (package **`aish`**: `Run`, `Execute`, `NewManager`) → `internal/ai-ssh/<cmd>` (closed loop per subcommand) → `internal/pkg/*` (shared, no product subcommand ownership).

**Directory vs package:** `internal/ai-ssh/` uses Go package `aish` (`ai-ssh` is not a valid identifier). Subcommand dirs still use package names matching Cobra (`login`, `shell`, …).

## Subcommand package (`internal/ai-ssh/<cmd>/`)

One package per top-level command owns: `Name`, `flags.go`, `parse.go`, `cmd.go` (`New`), `help.go`, `run.go`, **`register.go`** (`init` → `registry.Register`).

- **No** `internal/pkg/aitcmd` or names-only constant packages.
- **No** thin `internal/ai-ssh/<cmd>/` wrappers with parse elsewhere (one closed-loop package per command).

## Registry (OCP)

- Root: `registry.AttachRoot` in `internal/ai-ssh/cli_root.go`; root help via `registry.RootHelpEntries()` / `pkg/helpdoc.WriteRootHelp`（[`registry/root_help.go`](internal/ai-ssh/registry/root_help.go)）。
- **Do not** hand-edit `AddCommand` lists for new top-level or nested commands.
- New top-level: `internal/ai-ssh/<cmd>/` + `_ "…/registry/all/imports.go"`.
- Nested (`ai-ssh ai`, `ai-ssh config`, `provider`, `ollama`): parent `<parent>/subregistry` + child `register.go` + `<parent>/registry/all/imports.go`.

## Package name = command name

**Exception:** `internal/ai-ssh/` root is package **`aish`** (directory `ai-ssh`). Otherwise directory/package = Cobra name (`login`, `ai/ask`, `config/set`). No `*cmd` package suffix. AI REPL: `internal/ai-ssh/ai/mode`. CLI `session`: `internal/ai-ssh/session` (alias pkg session as `pkgsession`).

## `helpdoc`

- Shared: `internal/pkg/helpdoc`. Per-command: `internal/ai-ssh/<cmd>/help.go` (nested: `<parent>/<sub>/help.go`).

## `clihints` (Try SSOT)

- Shared errhint Try example lines: [`internal/pkg/clihints`](internal/pkg/clihints/try_lines.go).
- `internal/ai-ssh` and `internal/pkg/ssh/*` reference `clihints` constants; do not duplicate literals such as `ai-ssh session --list`.

## `internal/pkg`

- Shared OpenSSH argv: `internal/pkg/ssh/openssh`.
- **Must not** import `internal/ai-ssh`.
- Meta `!ai-ssh get`/`put`: protocol names in `internal/pkg/ssh/client/transfer` (`CmdGet`/`CmdPut`); test alignment with `get.Name` / `put.Name` in `internal/ai-ssh`.

## Refactors

Semantic unchanged; **R1–R19**, **A20–A22**; gate: `make fmt && make vet && make test && make build && make test-cross`.
